      "math_academy_id": "q-78570",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Consider a matrix equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x=B\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $7\\times 7$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $7\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x=B\\,d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}\\,x & =B\\,d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}\\,x & =AB\\,d \\\\ {I}_{7}\\,x & =AB\\,d \\\\ x & =AB\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
